diff --git a/docs/cli.md b/docs/cli.md
index b87951b..ed1b7a3 100644
--- a/docs/cli.md
+++ b/docs/cli.md
@@ -603,6 +603,138 @@ All five honor `--json`. `ext update` **exits non-zero** if any package failed
 
 ---
 
+## migrate — extension migrations
+
+```bash
+autosk migrate plan     <workflow> [--from <digest>]
+autosk migrate apply    <workflow> [--from <digest>]
+autosk migrate rollback <migration-id>
+autosk migrate list
+```
+
+Manage extension migrations — the mechanism that moves a task's runtime
+identity pin from one extension distribution digest to another. Use it when an
+extension update lands and the open tasks need to move to the new bytes.
+
+- `plan` — show what a migration would do (no writes). Prints the source and
+  target digests and every task that would move, or the reason it is refused.
+- `apply` — execute the migration. Moves each task's pin and seals a receipt
+  (crash-safe, resumable, read-back verified). Prints the receipt id and the
+  sealed timestamp.
+- `rollback` — reverse a completed migration. The operator must have restored
+  the previous distribution first (e.g. re-installed the old extension); the
+  daemon checks this and returns the reason if the registry still serves the
+  migrated-to digest.
+- `list` — show the project's migration receipts, newest first (`ID FROM TO
+  WORKFLOW TASKS SEALED REVERSING`).
+
+`--from` is optional: when omitted, the daemon infers the single source digest
+from the open tasks of that workflow. If several digests are present
+(mid-migration), it must be named explicitly. Closed tasks keep their last pin
+but never take part in a migration, so they do not count toward that
+ambiguity.
+
+`rollback` accepts a unique id prefix — `migrate list` displays one — and
+refuses an ambiguous or unknown one rather than guessing.
+
+All four honor `--json`. Exit codes:
+
+- `0` — success (an empty `migrate list` is a success with zero rows).
+- `1` — failure: transport or daemon error, or an apply/rollback that started
+  and could not finish (the receipt stays open; see below).
+- `2` — refusal: the daemon answered but declined the operation. In `--json`
+  mode the refusal result is printed to stdout first, so a script can read
+  `supported`/`reason` or `ok`/`reason` and still branch on the code.
+
+**Continuation.** A migration that dies between `apply` and its seal leaves an
+*open receipt* — `migrate list` shows it with `SEALED` = `open`. The next
+`autosk migrate apply <workflow>` does not re-plan: it finds the open receipt
+and finishes exactly that migration (re-planning over the remaining tasks
+would name a different migration). The same holds for an interrupted
+`rollback`. `apply` refuses rather than guess when several receipts are open,
+when `--from` does not match the open receipt's source, or when the workflow
+no longer serves the receipt's target — restore the target distribution or
+resolve the open receipts first.
+
+**Refusals** (exit `2`). `plan` and `apply` decline when:
+
+- no open tasks of the workflow are pinned to a distribution and `--from` is
+  not given — `no open tasks pinned to a distribution for workflow <w>`;
+- the open tasks are pinned to more than one distribution — `open tasks are
+  pinned to N distributions for <w>; name --from`;
+- the source digest is not recorded — `source distribution <d> is not recorded`;
+- the distribution the workflow serves is not recorded — `target distribution
+  <d> is not recorded`;
+- the workflow has no registered distribution — `<w> has no identified
+  distribution to migrate to`, or `<w> is not registered`;
+- the workflow already serves the source — `<w> already serves <d>`;
+- a task's step does not exist in the target — `N task(s) cannot move: <id>:
+  <step> does not exist in the target`;
+- an open task's runtime identity pin is unreadable — `cannot read the pin of
+  N open task(s)`;
+- a task's pin and its position name different workflows — `N open task(s)
+  name different workflows in their pin and their position`;
+- receipts are already open — `N migrations are still open for <w>`;
+- `--from` does not match the open receipt — `open migration <id> moves from
+  <from>, not <f>`;
+- the open receipt's target is not served any more, in any of its three
+  recorded components — `open migration <id> targets <to>, but <w> serves
+  <served>` (distribution), `open migration <id> declares graph <g>, but <w>
+  serves <g'>` (declared shape), or `open migration <id> declares document
+  <d>, but <w> serves <d'>` (target document; checked only when the receipt
+  records one), or `has no identified distribution` when the workflow serves
+  nothing.
+
+`rollback` declines when:
+
+- the id names no migration — `migration <id> was never opened`;
+- the prefix matches several — `migration id <id> is ambiguous (N matches)`;
+- the migration was never sealed — `migration <id> is not completed, there is
+  nothing settled to reverse`;
+- the registry still serves the migrated-to distribution, or serves neither —
+  `rolling back <id> needs <w> to serve <from>; it serves <served>`;
+- several reversals of the same migration are open — `N rollbacks of <id> are
+  still open`;
+- an open reversal cannot continue — the same `cannot continue`, `targets`,
+  `declares graph`, and `declares document` refusals as `apply`;
+- the reverse plan hits any of the planner refusals listed for `plan`/`apply`
+  above, evaluated on the reverse direction (the original's `to` as source,
+  the original's `from` as target) — including unrecorded distributions,
+  stranded or unreadably pinned tasks, and split workflow pins.
+
+**Known limitation.** `resume` on a migrated task fails with
+`extension_version_mismatch: <w> has no recorded store helper for this task` —
+`apply` drops the helper half of the pin (a separate recorded defect, not this
+command's doing). The remedy is `autosk enroll <task> --workflow <w>` (lands
+on the workflow's first step; `--step` names another) and then `resume`; the
+task continues on the migrated distribution.
+
+```text
+$ autosk migrate plan feature-dev
+migration a1b2c3… → d4e5f6… (feature-dev)
+  3 task(s) to move:
+    ask-489315 [review]
+    ask-7a2b1c [dev]
+    ask-f8e3d4 [intake]
+
+$ autosk migrate apply feature-dev
+migration a1b2c3 applied (3 task(s))
+  a1b2c3… → d4e5f6…
+  sealed at 2026-09-17 09:42:11
+
+$ autosk migrate rollback a1b2c3d4e5f6…
+rollback b7c8d9 applied (3 task(s))
+  d4e5f6… → a1b2c3… (reverses a1b2c3…)
+  sealed at 2026-09-17 09:44:03
+```
+
+For the discovery/digest model and what a distribution digest names, see
+[docs/extensions.md](extensions.md). For the write-API design contract that
+keeps the CLI over the same API, see
+[docs/contracts/sdk-write-api.md](../contracts/sdk-write-api.md) §7.
+
